A||N||5||Fiero5||4 cyl. won't start on it's own||||1||
Z||000000||Fiero5||02-25-2001||03:40 PM||||Hi there fellow Fiero lovers :o)<P>Here is a good one that everyone can put their thinking caps on for...<BR>We are trying to get Fiero1 back on the road. It is an 84SE 4 cyl. She<BR>will start and run great, BUT only if you squirt some gas in the carb<BR>first before turning the key. She won't start on her own. We have been<BR>swapping parts from Fiero10 which is an 84 base model 4cyl., to see what<BR>parts work and what do not.<BR>My father says that the fuses in Fiero1 are fine, the relay works fine and<BR>obviously the fual pump works fine as the engine will run great once you<BR>squirt some gas in the carb first to get it going. <BR>When you turn the key, you do not hear the fuel pump whir on. My dad is<BR>assuming that maybe a wire somewhere is bad, as it doesn't seem to be<BR>getting power to feed the carb gas for startup.<BR>Again, once we get it running via squirting gas in the carb first, it will<BR>run fine all day long, until you turn it back off again :o(<BR>Any help is greatly appreciated.<P>Steve & Russ Kelley||||reg||1
Z||000001||TheFiero64||02-25-2001||03:59 PM||||Check the General chat. I gave some advice on the topic.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||02-25-2001||04:00 PM||||84 has enough diferances I don't know what's the same most of the time wiring wise.<P>ALDL terminal G on most years is the test point for the fuel pump. put a test ligh on it and turn the key on. If the bulb doesn't light there is no power to the pump. Since the car runs once there is oil pressure either the relay is bad, the wiring is bad, or the ECM is bad. (Don't count on the new relay being good.)<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fiero5||02-25-2001||04:19 PM||||Theogre, can you be more specific on the ALDL and terminal G? The repair manual doesn't seem to reference this anywhere that we could find.<BR>Any specific details on this would be greatly appreciated.<P>Josh, we don't seem to have a fusible link anywhere, (unless it is possibly below on the starter) so we can't go any further with that particular suggestion.<BR>Thanks everyone for the suggestions so far. keep 'em coming :o)||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||02-26-2001||07:49 PM||||you tie a test light between G and ground. be careful not to bugger the terminal.<P>You problem has nothing to do with fuse links or anything else. stop looking.<P>it's running once the car has oil pressure. the means either the relay, the relay wiring, or the ECM has quit. The drawing for this circuit is in all the manuals. In the haynes and most other books it's the drawing tittled "Electronic Fuel Injection (motor type) Fuel Control." The V6 and older 4 cyl use basically the same circuit to run the pump.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fiero5||02-26-2001||10:16 PM||||Well, I have to say that Fiero64 - good ole' Josh was right on the money!!! He called it first.<BR>My Dad took another look, and way down under where you could hardly see was a wire hanging. He spliced in a new wire and re-wired it back to the Pos+ and away she went! Fired right up!! Wahoooo!<P>Thanks Josh - You da man!<P>Now if we can just get it down off the bank and out of all the snow! Whew, we are exhausted from shoveling! Those things have a low underbelly :o) We have it half way down off the bank, but it keeps getting bogged in the snow and we all got bushed shoveling for the night.||||reg||6
